flowchart LR
  accTitle: Processing element — MAC and operand forwarding
  accDescr: Signed a_in and b_in feed a combinational multiplier and independent forwarding registers. The natural-width product is sign-extended before addition to the accumulator. All three registers share synchronous reset, clear priority, and enable. The accumulator feeds back into the adder and holds C at this PE.

  ai["a_in<br/>signed DATA_W<br/>from left"]
  bi["b_in<br/>signed DATA_W<br/>from above"]
  subgraph pe["pe (i, j)"]
    ar["A forwarding register<br/>DATA_W bits<br/>a_out ← a_in<br/>→ right, 1 enabled cycle"]
    br["B forwarding register<br/>DATA_W bits<br/>b_out ← b_in<br/>→ down, 1 enabled cycle"]
    subgraph mac["mac"]
      mul["Signed multiplier<br/>a_in × b_in<br/>2 × DATA_W bits"]
      ext["Sign extension<br/>2 × DATA_W → ACC_W"]
      add(("+"))
      acc["Accumulator register<br/>signed ACC_W; acc = C[i][j]<br/>acc ← acc + product"]
      mul --> ext --> add --> acc
      acc -->|"feedback"| add
    end
    rule["At each rising clk edge, for ALL registers:<br/>1. !rst_n or clear → zero<br/>2. else en → update<br/>3. else → hold"]
    rule -.-> ar
    rule -.-> br
    rule -.-> acc
  end
  ai --> mul
  bi --> mul
  ai --> ar
  bi --> br
  classDef reg fill:#e6f4ee,stroke:#34735a,color:#13263d
  classDef note fill:#fff3d6,stroke:#8b6016,color:#13263d
  class ar,br,acc reg
  class rule note
